<title>HUNGARY: FORECAST-HUNGARY GOVT PAPER YIELDS SEEN DOWN.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-HUNGARY GOVT PAPER YIELDS SEEN DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central bank's reduction of</p>
<p>most of its repo rates today will push yields down for short</p>
<p>maturities at this week's treasury bill auctions but will only</p>
<p>marginally effect the longer maturities, dealers said.</p>
<p>The National Bank of Hungary said earlier on Monday that</p>
<p>it cut its overnight repo, one-week repo, one-week reverse repo</p>
<p>and one-month reverse repo rates by 0.5 percentage points each.</p>
<p>The government debt management agency (AKK) will auction</p>
<p>one-month T-bills on Tuesday, three-month T-bills on Wednesday,</p>
<p>and six-month T-bills on Thursday and 12-month T-bills on</p>
<p>Friday.</p>
<p>				 T-BILLS		</p>
<p>		   ONE-MONTH   THREE-MONTH   SIX-MONTH    12-MONTH</p>
